# m3OS Phase 69 — m3os-term terminfo entry.
#
# Compiled to a binary entry via `tic -o <staging>/usr/share/terminfo` in
# xtask `populate_ext2_files`. Installed to
# `/usr/share/terminfo/m/m3os-term` inside the ext2 data disk so any
# program calling `setupterm()` or `tigetstr()` against
# `TERM=m3os-term` finds the right escape sequences.
#
# Capability set covers what `term` actually implements after Phase 69:
#   - 256-color SGR (Track C) + RGB truecolor extension
#   - Alternate-screen buffer ?1049 (Track B)
#   - DECSCUSR cursor shapes 0..=6 (Track F)
#   - Bracketed paste ?2004 (Track G)
#   - SGR mouse 1006 (Track E)
#   - Cursor movement / ED / EL / SGR (Phase 22b baseline)
#
# Capabilities that rely on non-CSI escape sequences (e.g. `ESC 7`,
# `ESC 8`, `ESC M`, `ESC c`, `ESC =`, `ESC >`, `ESC (` charset selects)
# are intentionally omitted because `kernel_core::fb::AnsiParser` only
# recognises `ESC [` (CSI) and silently discards everything else. The
# parser will be extended in a later phase; until then advertising
# those capabilities would mislead `setupterm()` callers.
#
# A small number of CSI capabilities (`csr`, `dch`, `dl`, `ech`, `ich`,
# `il`, `rin`, `indn`, `tbc`, `vpa`, `cbt`) remain in the entry: they
# parse cleanly today but route to a no-op in `dispatch_csi`. They are
# kept here so the published terminfo stays stable across the planned
# Phase 69+ work that wires the missing dispatch arms; a follow-up
# audit will either implement or remove each one as the parser grows.

m3os-term|m3OS Phase 69 terminal,
	am, bce, msgr, npc, xenl,
	colors#256, cols#80, it#8, lines#25, pairs#32767,
	bel=^G, blink=\E[5m, bold=\E[1m,
	cbt=\E[Z, civis=\E[?25l, clear=\E[H\E[2J, cnorm=\E[?25h,
	cr=\r, csr=\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dr, cub=\E[%p1%dD, cub1=\b,
	cud=\E[%p1%dB, cud1=\n, cuf=\E[%p1%dC, cuf1=\E[C,
	cup=\E[%i%p1%d;%p2%dH, cuu=\E[%p1%dA, cuu1=\E[A,
	dch=\E[%p1%dP, dch1=\E[P, dl=\E[%p1%dM, dl1=\E[M,
	ech=\E[%p1%dX, ed=\E[J, el=\E[K, el1=\E[1K,
	enacs=, home=\E[H, hpa=\E[%i%p1%dG, ht=^I,
	ich=\E[%p1%d@, il=\E[%p1%dL, il1=\E[L,
	ind=\n, indn=\E[%p1%dS,
	invis=\E[8m, kbs=\b, kcbt=\E[Z, kcub1=\EOD, kcud1=\EOB,
	kcuf1=\EOC, kcuu1=\EOA, kdch1=\E[3~, kend=\EOF, khome=\EOH,
	kich1=\E[2~, kmous=\E[<, knp=\E[6~, kpp=\E[5~,
	op=\E[39;49m, rev=\E[7m,
	rin=\E[%p1%dT, rmcup=\E[?1049l,
	rmso=\E[27m, rmul=\E[24m,
	setab=\E[%?%p1%{8}%<%t4%p1%d%e%p1%{16}%<%t10%p1%{8}%-%d%e48;5;%p1%d%;m,
	setaf=\E[%?%p1%{8}%<%t3%p1%d%e%p1%{16}%<%t9%p1%{8}%-%d%e38;5;%p1%d%;m,
	sgr=\E[0%?%p6%t;1%;%?%p2%t;4%;%?%p1%p3%|%t;7%;%?%p4%t;5%;m,
	sgr0=\E[0m, smcup=\E[?1049h,
	smso=\E[7m, smul=\E[4m, tbc=\E[3g,
	u6=\E[%i%d;%dR, u7=\E[6n, u8=\E[?%[;0123456789]c, u9=\E[c,
	vpa=\E[%i%p1%dd,
	BE=\E[?2004h, BD=\E[?2004l,
	XM=\E[?1006;1000%?%p1%{1}%=%th%el%;,
	Ss=\E[%p1%d\sq, Se=\E[2\sq,
